{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1788369687,"nonce":"OfU9nfITECVI6d04wsbWgiPo+74=","message":"**CLOSED — built, merged and run by the orchestrator, 2026-09-02.** Merged at `94dd604`, plus `1202796` for a defect found on first real use.\n\n```\n$ ./cockpit/cockpit m1-20260901 --probe\nchain     5 segment(s): m1-20260901 -\u003e -s00 -\u003e -s01 -\u003e -s02 -\u003e -s03\nsteps     4,599        days 0..67        map-views 10\nno result 3            ok/error 3,908 / 691\n\n$ python3 cockpit/verify-readonly.py m1-20260901 --seconds 20\nfiles before 15460   after 15460\ncommands/ + results/ gained   0 file(s)   PASS\nnew transcript step dirs      PASS (0)\naudit hook violations         0           PASS      exit 0\n```\n\nAcceptance item 2 — the real deliverable — is proven twice over, and the second half is the stronger one: a `sys.addaudithook` that fails on any write-mode `open`, socket, subprocess, unlink, rename or mkdir. A directory diff observes that nothing changed; the audit hook proves **the process wrote nothing**, which is not confoundable. Its static argument about the watermark checks out: `Journal.NoteRead` has exactly one caller (`JournalVerbs.cs:219`), reachable only through `Poller.ScanInbox` finding a file in `commands/`, and `commands/` gained nothing.\n\n**A defect found by using it, which no headless capture could have caught.** `Cockpit.__init__` stored the transcript as `self.run`, shadowing Textual's `App.run()`, so `app.run()` raised `TypeError: 'Run' object is not callable` the instant it was started interactively. Every screenshot used the headless driver, which enters through a different path — so the only path a human uses was the only path never exercised. The worker had declared exactly this in its \"did NOT demonstrate\" section, which is how it took one look to find. Fixed in `1202796` and verified under a pty: no traceback, 122KB of screen output, map/journal/step regions painting.\n\nAlso in `1202796`: `cockpit/launch-cockpit.sh`, because a window-manager `exec` inherits no working directory and the first launch died on a relative path before Python started.\n\nRun live on the bench in `--follow` mode against a growing transcript while the orchestrator drove acceptance.\n\n\n- **`3d53df2`** — transcript step order is *claim* order, not completion order: 141 inverted adjacent pairs, and 78 of 489 advances have a next step that returned earlier. `accept/4.2-play-loop.py`'s `advance_discipline` reasons about adjacency, so it grades an adjacency that did not happen.\n- Following `meta.json` links alone yields **999 of 4,599 steps (21.7%)**, because the existing segments carry no links and `rwa` derives them only on open — which is a write. It derives siblings by name instead.\n- Page two: **133 verbs, 71 used, 62 never called.** The whole `dev:` surface dark is correct discipline; `quest*`, `policy*`, `orders`, `repair` and `schedule` dark across 66 days is not.\n\n\n**No rendering was reviewed in a real terminal emulator by the author** — every committed capture is Textual's headless driver, which is exactly what hid the shadowing bug. The orchestrator has since run it under a pty and in kitty. Size came in at ~1,090 code lines against a 400–600 target; the worker flagged this and stopped rather than pushing through, and roughly 120 of the overage is the second page added mid-flight.","files":null}]}